[1811.338, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m (PRE=1 build/exp/run.sh g800b 1.25 0 0101 1 1000 0 kogge-stone & PRE=1 build/exp/run.sh g400 2.5 0 0100 0 2000 0 kogge-stone & wait) 2>&1 | grep -v Warning; grep -E \"ERROR|before|^worst|RSZ-00(45|51)\" build/exp/g800b/rsz.log | head; build/exp/path.sh build/exp/g800b/sta.rpt | head -30\r\ng400 P=2.5 enc=0 csa=0100 spl=0 abcD=2000 | yosys_area=2381.764000 rsz_area=2387 wns=0.152 whs=0.053 pwr_est=6.5253e-04\r\ng800b P=1.25 enc=0 csa=0101 spl=1 abcD=1000 | yosys_area=3199.448000 rsz_area=4182 wns=-0.729 whs=0.028 pwr_est=1.9929e-03\r\n== before: -1.239 ns\r\n[INFO RSZ-0045] Inserted 77 buffers, 77 to split loads.\r\n[INFO RSZ-0051] Resized 897 instances: 897 up, 0 up match, 0 down, 0 VT\r\nworst slack max -0.73\r\nworst slack min 0.03\r\nby clk) fo=Startpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\nby clk) fo=Endpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\n_3202_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=5 d=0.459 t=0.459\r\n_2059_/Z (XOR2_X2) fo=2 d=0.211 t=0.670\r\n_2060_/ZN (AND2_X2) fo=1 d=0.117 t=0.788\r\n_2061_/ZN (AOI222_X2) fo=2 d=0.059 t=0.847\r\n_2065_/ZN (AOI221_X2) fo=2 d=0.394 t=1.241\r\n_2099_/ZN (OAI21_X2) fo=3 d=0.129 t=1.370\r\n_2100_/ZN (NAND2_X2) fo=2 d=0.100 t=1.470\r\n_2101_/ZN (OAI22_X1) fo=2 d=0.074 t=1.544\r\n_2105_/ZN (OR3_X4) fo=1 d=0.278 t=1.822\r\n_2106_/ZN (AOI21_X4) fo=1 d=0.097 t=1.919\r\n                                     1.919   data arrival time\r\n                           -0.060    1.190   library setup time\r\n                                    -1.919   data arrival time\r\nslack (VIOLATED) fo=-0.729 d= t=\r\n"]
[1893.456, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 1,400p SPEC.md | head -c 30000; ls submission/rtl_400 submission/scripts; cat Makefile\r\n# mkMultBuff Design Specification\r\n\r\nPipelined signed 16 \u00d7 16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer\r\n\r\n## 1. Scope\r\n\r\nThis document specifies `mkMultBuff`, a pipelined multiplier for 16-bit two's-complement operands. Its 32-bit products are stored in an external 64-entry memory and returned to a consumer in the order in which they were produced. Two implementations of the same interface are required, one closing timing at 400 MHz and one at 800 MHz.\r\n\r\n## 2. Conventions\r\n\r\nAll registers are clocked on the rising edge of `clk`, and every cycle-level statement refers to signal values sampled at a rising edge. Requirements use \"shall\" and carry an identifier for traceability.\r\n\r\n| Term | Definition |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Accepted operand pair | Operands present in a cycle in which `EN_mult` = 1 and `RDY_mult` = 1 |\r\n| Accepted read | A read request in a cycle in which `EN_blockRead` = 1 and `RDY_blockRead` = 1 |\r\n| Fill phase | The interval from reset, or from the end of a drain phase, to the write of the 64th product |\r\n| Drain phase | The interval from the assertion of `RDY_blockRead` to the acceptance of the 64th read |\r\n| Latency | The number of cycles from the acceptance of an operand pair to the write of its product |\r\n\r\n## 3. Interface\r\n\r\nThe port list is fixed and defined in `starter/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv`, with N = 32.\r\n\r\n| Port | Direction | Width | Description |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `clk` | input | 1 | Clock |\r\n| `RST_N` | input | 1 | Synchronous reset, active low |\r\n| `EN_mult` | input | 1 | The producer presents a valid operand pair |\r\n| `mult_input0`, `mult_input1` | input | 16 | Operands, two's complement |\r\n| `RDY_mult` | output | 1 | The block can accept an operand pair |\r\n| `EN_blockRead` | input | 1 | The consumer requests a product |\r\n| `RDY_blockRead` | output | 1 | The block can accept a read |\r\n| `VALID_memVal` | output | 1 | `memVal_data` carries a product |\r\n| `memVal_data` | output | N | Product returned to the consumer |\r\n| `EN_writeMem` | output | 1 | Memory write enable |\r\n| `writeMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory write address |\r\n| `writeMem_val` | output | N | Memory write data |\r\n| `EN_readMem` | output | 1 | Memory read enable |\r\n| `readMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory read address |\r\n| `readMem_val` | input | N | Memory read data |\r\n\r\nThe memory, `starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv`, is a 64 \u00d7 N two-port array instantiated in the testbench. It is not part of `mkMultBuff` and is excluded from synthesis. A write stores `writeMem_val` at a rising edge at which `EN_writeMem` = 1. A read registers the addressed word at a rising edge at which `EN_readMem` = 1, so `readMem_val` is valid in the following cycle.\r\n\r\n## 4. Functional requirements\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Datapath\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F1 | Each accepted operand pair shall produce exactly one memory write, whose data is the 32-bit two's-complement product of `mult_input0` and `mult_input1`. |\r\n| F2 | Products shall be written in acceptance order to consecutive addresses, starting at address 0 in each fill phase. |\r\n| F3 | The multiplier shall be fully pipelined and sustain a throughput of one operand pair per cycle. |\r\n| F4 | The latency is implementation-defined. `EN_writeMem` shall be asserted only in cycles in which `writeMem_addr` and `writeMem_val` carry a valid address and product. |\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Fill\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F5 | `RDY_mult` shall be 1 if and only if no drain phase is in progress and fewer than 64 operand pairs have been accepted in the current fill phase. Operand pairs in flight therefore count against the capacity of the memory. `EN_mult` shall have no effect while `RDY_mult` is 0. |\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Transition to drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F6 | `RDY_blockRead` shall be asserted in the cycle following the write to address 63 and shall remain asserted until the 64th read is accepted. |\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F7 | In each cycle in which a read is accepted, `EN_readMem` shall be 1 and `readMem_addr` shall hold the next sequential address, starting at 0. |\r\n| F8 | `VALID_memVal` shall be 1 in, and only in, the cycle following each accepted read. In that cycle `memVal_data` shall equal `readMem_val`, which shall not be registered again inside `mkMultBuff`. |\r\n| F9 | `EN_blockRead` shall have no effect while `RDY_blockRead` is 0. |\r\n| F10 | In the cycle following the accepted read of address 63, `RDY_blockRead` shall be 0 and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. |\r\n\r\n### 4.5 Flow control and invariants\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F11 | The block shall operate correctly for any sequence of `EN_mult` and `EN_blockRead`. Deasserting either signal stalls the corresponding transfer without loss or duplication of data. |\r\n| F12 | `RDY_mult` and `RDY_blockRead` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n| F13 | `EN_writeMem` and `EN_readMem` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n\r\n### 4.6 Reset\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F14 | Every register shall have a synchronous, active-low reset driven by `RST_N`. |\r\n| F15 | In the cycle following a rising edge at which `RST_N` = 0, no product shall be in flight or stored and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. `EN_writeMem`, `writeMem_addr`, `RDY_blockRead`, `EN_readMem` and `VALID_memVal` shall be 0. |\r\n\r\nFigures 1 to 4 illustrate the phases of operation for an implementation with a latency of two cycles.\r\n\r\n![Figure 1. Fill phase](docs/fig/fill.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 2. Memory full and transition to drain](docs/fig/full.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 3. Drain phase](docs/fig/drain.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 4. End of drain phase](docs/fig/drain_end.svg)\r\n\r\n## 5. Implementation targets\r\n\r\n| Parameter | 400 MHz implementation | 800 MHz implementation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Source directory | `submission/rtl_400/` | `submission/rtl_800/` |\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns | 1.25 ns |\r\n| Pipeline stages | 2 minimum | Implementation-defined |\r\n| Worst slack, required | \u2265 0 ps | \u2265 0 ps |\r\n| Worst slack, target | \u2265 125 ps (5 % of period) | \u2265 62 ps (5 % of period) |\r\n| Cell area | < 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2 | < 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n| Power | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity |\r\n\r\nEach implementation shall have `mkMultBuff` as its top module and shall compile from the complete set of `.sv` files in its source directory, read in any order. `` `include`` directives shall not be used. The targets apply to the results of the open-source flow in Section 7. The slack target leaves margin for physical implementation. Among implementations that meet timing and area, lower area and lower power are preferred.\r\n\r\n## 6. Technology and constraints\r\n\r\nThe open-source flow targets the Nangate45 Open Cell Library, which is built on the FreePDK45 process, at its slowest available corner. The install script written under Section 7 shall obtain the library from a public source, which the report shall identify together with the corner used. The library is not stored in this repository.\r\n\r\nFor comparison with designs built on the GPDK045 library, the sign-off service of Section 8.3 synthesizes the submitted RTL with GPDK045 and simulates the resulting netlists. Its results are reported alongside those of the open-source flow, not in place of them.\r\n\r\n| Constraint | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns or 1.25 ns |\r\n| Input delay, all inputs except `clk` | 0 ns |\r\n| Output delay, all outputs | 0 ns |\r\n| Input drive | Output of the smallest D flip-flop in the library |\r\n| Input transition | One eighth of the clock period |\r\n| Output load | Four times the capacitance of one input of the library's X4 two-input NAND (`NAND2_X4` in Nangate45) |\r\n\r\nSynthesis may target a shorter internal clock period and may retime registers. All reported figures are evaluated at the target period.\r\n\r\n## 7. Tool flow\r\n\r\nThe flow shall use open-source tools only and shall be reproducible on a clean Linux host through an install script in the repository. Each step is invoked from the repository root as `make <step> RUN=<400|800>`.\r\n\r\n| Step | Function | Output |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `synth` | Synthesis of `submission/rtl_<RUN>/` to the target library | Netlist and SDF in `submission/outputs/`; reports in `submission/syn_reports/` |\r\n| `check` | RTL simulation with the RTL checker | Simulation log ending in `ALL PASS` |\r\n| `sim` | Gate-level simulation of the netlist with the RTL checker, without back-annotation | Value change dump (VCD) |\r\n| `timing` | Gate-level simulation with SDF back-annotation and the gate-level checker | Simulation log reporting `ALL PASS` or `TIMING FAIL` |\r\n| `power` | Activity-based power analysis from the VCD | Power report |\r\n\r\nOpen-source code and optimization techniques may be used where their licenses permit, with each source cited in the report. Complete implementations of this specification from other sources shall not be used.\r\n\r\n## 8. Verification requirements\r\n\r\nThe harnesses in `starter/tb/` instantiate the design and the memory and generate the clock.\r\n\r\n### 8.1 RTL checker\r\n\r\nThe RTL checker, `submission/testbench/rtl_checker.sv` with top module `mkMultBuff_tb`, shall\r\n\r\n- run at least eight complete fill and drain phases\r\n- drive operands from a random source, in addition to the directed pairs (\u221232768, \u221232768), (\u22121, 1), (0, 32767), (32767, 32767) and (\u22121, \u22121)\r\n- deassert `EN_mult` within a fill phase and `EN_blockRead` within a drain phase\r\n- compare every product returned on `memVal_data` with an independent reference model\r\n- check every observable requirement of Section 4\r\n- print `ALL PASS` if and only if no check has failed\r\n\r\nThe stimulus shall also contain one fill phase with `EN_mult` held at 1 for 64 consecutive cycles and one drain phase with `EN_blockRead` held at 1 for 64 consecutive cycles. These windows are used for power analysis.\r\n\r\n### 8.2 Gate-level checkers\r\n\r\nThe gate-level checkers, `submission/testbench/sdf_checker_400.sv` and `sdf_checker_800.sv` with top modules `mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_400` and `mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_800`, simulate the synthesized netlist with SDF back-annotation at fixed clock periods of 2.5 ns and 1.25 ns. The SDF file is supplied as `+sdf_file=<path>`. Each checker shall\r\n\r\n- drive inputs after the rising edge and sample outputs at the falling edge\r\n- apply random operands over multiple fill and drain phases\r\n- report `TIMING FAIL` for any unknown (X) or incorrect value on `memVal_data` while `VALID_memVal` is 1\r\n- print `ALL PASS` if and only if no failure has occurred\r\n\r\nEach checker shall pass a netlist that meets timing and fail a netlist that violates it. Both outcomes shall be demonstrated and their logs retained. Where the available cell models or simulator do not turn a timing violation into an unknown value, the checker shall detect the violation through the resulting incorrect values, and the report shall describe the limitation.\r\n\r\n### 8.3 Sign-off service\r\n\r\nPushing a branch named `check/<label>` submits the RTL in `submission/rtl_400/` and `submission/rtl_800/` to an independent sign-off service. The latest commit on the branch is checked after each push. The service synthesizes each implementation with GPDK045 under the constraints of Section 6 and simulates the resulting netlists with SDF back-annotation against an independent testbench. Its scorecard is published on branch `check-results`.\r\n\r\n## 9. Deliverables\r\n\r\n```\r\nsubmission/\r\n  rtl_400/       400 MHz implementation\r\n  rtl_800/       800 MHz implementation\r\n  scripts/       synthesis and flow scripts\r\n  testbench/     rtl_checker.sv, sdf_checker_400.sv, sdf_checker_800.sv\r\n  outputs/       synthesis outputs\r\n  syn_reports/   synthesis and power reports\r\n  pdf_report/    report.pdf\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe report shall contain\r\n\r\n1. area and power at both frequencies, as a synthesis estimate and from activity-based analysis\r\n2. the pipeline depth and the critical path at each frequency\r\n3. the changes made to meet 800 MHz\r\n4. a state diagram of every state machine and a datapath diagram showing each pipeline stage and its registers\r\n5. a description of each checker, comparing RTL and gate-level waveforms and identifying effects that appear only at gate level, such as clock-to-output delay and glitches on `RDY_mult`\r\n6. the optimization techniques applied and their measured effect\r\n7. a description of the tool flow and of any departure from the constraints of Section 6\r\n8. a comparison of the open-source results with the GPDK045 sign-off results\r\n9. the external sources used, with citations\r\n10. the source listing, as an appendix\r\n\r\nThe report is generated by the implementing agent and shall be identified as AI-generated on its first page.\r\nsubmission/rtl_400:\r\nmkMultBuff.sv\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\n\r\nsubmission/scripts:\r\nabc_speed.script\r\nconstraints.tcl\r\ninstall.sh\r\nmutate.sh\r\npower.sh\r\npower.tcl\r\npower_summary.py\r\nresize.tcl\r\nsdf_typmax.py\r\nsta.tcl\r\nsynth.tcl\r\n# Makefile -- open-source flow for mkMultBuff (SPEC.md Section 7).\r\n# Usage: make <synth|check|sim|timing|power|all> RUN=<400|800>\r\n# Toolchain: bash submission/scripts/install.sh\r\n\r\nRUN      ?= 400\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 2.5\r\n  HALF    := 1.25\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 2200\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\nelse ifeq ($(RUN),800)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 1.25\r\n  HALF    := 0.625\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 1050\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\nelse\r\n  $(error RUN must be 400 or 800)\r\nendif\r\n\r\nROOT     := $(CURDIR)\r\nLIB      := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib\r\nCELLS    := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary.v\r\nRTL_DIR  ?= submission/rtl_$(RUN)\r\nRTL      := $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv)\r\nMEM      := starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv starter/rtl/registerArray.sv\r\nTB       := submission/testbench\r\nOUT      := submission/outputs\r\nREP      ?= submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)\r\nBUILD    ?= build/$(RUN)\r\nNETLIST  ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.v\r\nSDF      ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.sdf\r\nSEED     ?= 402\r\nSETUP_MARGIN ?= 0.15\r\n\r\nYOSYS_IMAGE := openroad/orfs@sha256:d3505fd5f930fcd20d3d25a41f3047230b7db7b7797e3448561c9e556cca3774\r\nSTA_IMAGE   := openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a\r\nDOCKER      := docker run --rm -v $(ROOT):$(ROOT) -w $(ROOT)\r\nYOSYS       := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e RTL_DIR=$(RTL_DIR) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e ABC_D=$(ABC_D) -e BOOTH=$(BOOTH) -e ADDER=$(ADDER) -e OUT=$(BUILD)/syn.v \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/yosys\r\nOPENROAD    := $(DOCKER) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST_IN=$(BUILD)/syn.v -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               -e SETUP_MARGIN=$(SETUP_MARGIN) -e PDK_LEF_DIR=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/nangate45/lef \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/OpenROAD/bin/openroad -no_init -exit\r\nSTA         := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e SDF=$(SDF) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta $(STA_IMAGE) -no_init -no_splash -exit\r\n\r\n.PHONY: synth check sim timing power all clean timing_fail sta_only\r\n\r\n$(REP) $(BUILD) $(OUT):\r\n\tmkdir -p $@\r\n\r\n# ---- synthesis + static timing (netlist, SDF, area/timing/power-estimate reports)\r\nsynth: | $(REP) $(OUT) $(BUILD)\r\n\t$(YOSYS) -q -l $(REP)/synth.log -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl\r\n\tmv -f $(BUILD)/syn.stat.rpt $(REP)/yosys_area.rpt\r\n\t$(OPENROAD) submission/scripts/resize.tcl > $(REP)/resize.log 2>&1\r\n\t$(STA) submission/scripts/sta.tcl > $(REP)/sta.rpt 2>&1\r\n\tpython3 submission/scripts/sdf_typmax.py $(SDF).sta $(SDF) && rm -f $(SDF).sta\r\n\t@grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns|Total|cell area)\" $(REP)/sta.rpt\r\n\r\n# ---- RTL simulation with the RTL checker\r\ncheck: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=$(HALF) -o $(BUILD)/check.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/rtl_checker.sv $(MEM) $(RTL)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/check.vvp +seed=$(SEED) | tee $(REP)/check.log | tail -25\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/check.log || { echo \"check FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# simulation copy of the netlist: the harness instantiates mkMultBuff #(.N(32)),\r\n# so an (unused) parameter N is declared in the netlist module\r\n$(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v: $(NETLIST) | $(BUILD)\r\n\tsed -e '0,/^module mkMultBuff (/s//module mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (/' $< > $@\r\n\r\n# ---- gate-level simulation (zero delay, no back-annotation) with the RTL checker -> VCD\r\nsim: $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=$(HALF) -o $(BUILD)/sim.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/rtl_checker.sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/sim.vvp +seed=$(SEED) +vcd=$(BUILD)/gate.vcd | tee $(REP)/sim.log | tail -25\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/sim.log || { echo \"sim FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# ---- gate-level simulation with SDF back-annotation and the gate-level checker\r\ntiming: $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -gspecify -s mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_$(RUN) -o $(BUILD)/timing.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/sdf_checker_$(RUN).sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/timing.vvp +sdf_file=$(SDF) +seed=$(SEED) > $(REP)/timing.log 2>&1 ; true\r\n\t@grep -v -i \"sdf.*warning\" $(REP)/timing.log | tail -12\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/timing.log || { echo \"timing FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# ---- activity-based power from the gate-level VCD (whole run and the two 64-cycle windows)\r\npower: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tbash submission/scripts/power.sh $(REP) $(BUILD) $(NETLIST) $(PERIOD) $(LIB) $(STA_IMAGE)\r\n\r\n# ---- demonstration that the gate-level checker fails a netlist that violates timing\r\n#  RUN=400: the one-stage-multiplier variant in submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage,\r\n#           synthesized with the same flow at 2.5 ns (STA reports negative slack)\r\n#  RUN=800: the 400 MHz netlist, timed by STA and back-annotated at 1.25 ns\r\nFAIL_BUILD := build/fail_$(RUN)\r\nFAIL_REP   := submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)/timing_fail\r\ntiming_fail:\r\n\tmkdir -p $(FAIL_BUILD) $(FAIL_REP)\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n\t$(MAKE) synth RUN=400 RTL_DIR=submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n\t    NETLIST=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.v SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\nelse\r\n\t$(MAKE) sta_only RUN=800 BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n\t    NETLIST=$(OUT)/mkMultBuff_400_map.v SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\nendif\r\n\t-$(MAKE) timing RUN=$(RUN) BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) NETLIST=$(if $(filter 400,$(RUN)),$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.v,$(OUT)/mkMultBuff_400_map.v) SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\n\t@grep -q \"TIMING FAIL\" $(FAIL_REP)/timing.log && echo \"timing_fail: checker reported TIMING FAIL as expected\" \\\r\n\t    || { echo \"timing_fail: checker did NOT fail\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\nsta_only: | $(REP)\r\n\t$(STA) submission/scripts/sta.tcl > $(REP)/sta.rpt 2>&1\r\n\tpython3 submission/scripts/sdf_typmax.py $(SDF).sta $(SDF) && rm -f $(SDF).sta\r\n\t@grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns)\" $(REP)/sta.rpt\r\n\r\nall: synth check sim timing power\r\n\r\nclean:\r\n\trm -rf build\r\n"]
[1893.542, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n 1,400p SPEC.md | head -c 30000; ls; ls submission/rtl_400 build 2>/dev/null\r\n# mkMultBuff Design Specification\r\n\r\nPipelined signed 16 \u00d7 16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer\r\n\r\n## 1. Scope\r\n\r\nThis document specifies `mkMultBuff`, a pipelined multiplier for 16-bit two's-complement operands. Its 32-bit products are stored in an external 64-entry memory and returned to a consumer in the order in which they were produced. Two implementations of the same interface are required, one closing timing at 400 MHz and one at 800 MHz.\r\n\r\n## 2. Conventions\r\n\r\nAll registers are clocked on the rising edge of `clk`, and every cycle-level statement refers to signal values sampled at a rising edge. Requirements use \"shall\" and carry an identifier for traceability.\r\n\r\n| Term | Definition |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Accepted operand pair | Operands present in a cycle in which `EN_mult` = 1 and `RDY_mult` = 1 |\r\n| Accepted read | A read request in a cycle in which `EN_blockRead` = 1 and `RDY_blockRead` = 1 |\r\n| Fill phase | The interval from reset, or from the end of a drain phase, to the write of the 64th product |\r\n| Drain phase | The interval from the assertion of `RDY_blockRead` to the acceptance of the 64th read |\r\n| Latency | The number of cycles from the acceptance of an operand pair to the write of its product |\r\n\r\n## 3. Interface\r\n\r\nThe port list is fixed and defined in `starter/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv`, with N = 32.\r\n\r\n| Port | Direction | Width | Description |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `clk` | input | 1 | Clock |\r\n| `RST_N` | input | 1 | Synchronous reset, active low |\r\n| `EN_mult` | input | 1 | The producer presents a valid operand pair |\r\n| `mult_input0`, `mult_input1` | input | 16 | Operands, two's complement |\r\n| `RDY_mult` | output | 1 | The block can accept an operand pair |\r\n| `EN_blockRead` | input | 1 | The consumer requests a product |\r\n| `RDY_blockRead` | output | 1 | The block can accept a read |\r\n| `VALID_memVal` | output | 1 | `memVal_data` carries a product |\r\n| `memVal_data` | output | N | Product returned to the consumer |\r\n| `EN_writeMem` | output | 1 | Memory write enable |\r\n| `writeMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory write address |\r\n| `writeMem_val` | output | N | Memory write data |\r\n| `EN_readMem` | output | 1 | Memory read enable |\r\n| `readMem_addr` | output | 6 | Memory read address |\r\n| `readMem_val` | input | N | Memory read data |\r\n\r\nThe memory, `starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv`, is a 64 \u00d7 N two-port array instantiated in the testbench. It is not part of `mkMultBuff` and is excluded from synthesis. A write stores `writeMem_val` at a rising edge at which `EN_writeMem` = 1. A read registers the addressed word at a rising edge at which `EN_readMem` = 1, so `readMem_val` is valid in the following cycle.\r\n\r\n## 4. Functional requirements\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Datapath\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F1 | Each accepted operand pair shall produce exactly one memory write, whose data is the 32-bit two's-complement product of `mult_input0` and `mult_input1`. |\r\n| F2 | Products shall be written in acceptance order to consecutive addresses, starting at address 0 in each fill phase. |\r\n| F3 | The multiplier shall be fully pipelined and sustain a throughput of one operand pair per cycle. |\r\n| F4 | The latency is implementation-defined. `EN_writeMem` shall be asserted only in cycles in which `writeMem_addr` and `writeMem_val` carry a valid address and product. |\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Fill\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F5 | `RDY_mult` shall be 1 if and only if no drain phase is in progress and fewer than 64 operand pairs have been accepted in the current fill phase. Operand pairs in flight therefore count against the capacity of the memory. `EN_mult` shall have no effect while `RDY_mult` is 0. |\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Transition to drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F6 | `RDY_blockRead` shall be asserted in the cycle following the write to address 63 and shall remain asserted until the 64th read is accepted. |\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Drain\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F7 | In each cycle in which a read is accepted, `EN_readMem` shall be 1 and `readMem_addr` shall hold the next sequential address, starting at 0. |\r\n| F8 | `VALID_memVal` shall be 1 in, and only in, the cycle following each accepted read. In that cycle `memVal_data` shall equal `readMem_val`, which shall not be registered again inside `mkMultBuff`. |\r\n| F9 | `EN_blockRead` shall have no effect while `RDY_blockRead` is 0. |\r\n| F10 | In the cycle following the accepted read of address 63, `RDY_blockRead` shall be 0 and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. |\r\n\r\n### 4.5 Flow control and invariants\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F11 | The block shall operate correctly for any sequence of `EN_mult` and `EN_blockRead`. Deasserting either signal stalls the corresponding transfer without loss or duplication of data. |\r\n| F12 | `RDY_mult` and `RDY_blockRead` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n| F13 | `EN_writeMem` and `EN_readMem` shall never be 1 in the same cycle. |\r\n\r\n### 4.6 Reset\r\n\r\n| ID | Requirement |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| F14 | Every register shall have a synchronous, active-low reset driven by `RST_N`. |\r\n| F15 | In the cycle following a rising edge at which `RST_N` = 0, no product shall be in flight or stored and `RDY_mult` shall be 1. `EN_writeMem`, `writeMem_addr`, `RDY_blockRead`, `EN_readMem` and `VALID_memVal` shall be 0. |\r\n\r\nFigures 1 to 4 illustrate the phases of operation for an implementation with a latency of two cycles.\r\n\r\n![Figure 1. Fill phase](docs/fig/fill.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 2. Memory full and transition to drain](docs/fig/full.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 3. Drain phase](docs/fig/drain.svg)\r\n\r\n![Figure 4. End of drain phase](docs/fig/drain_end.svg)\r\n\r\n## 5. Implementation targets\r\n\r\n| Parameter | 400 MHz implementation | 800 MHz implementation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Source directory | `submission/rtl_400/` | `submission/rtl_800/` |\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns | 1.25 ns |\r\n| Pipeline stages | 2 minimum | Implementation-defined |\r\n| Worst slack, required | \u2265 0 ps | \u2265 0 ps |\r\n| Worst slack, target | \u2265 125 ps (5 % of period) | \u2265 62 ps (5 % of period) |\r\n| Cell area | < 6000 \u00b5m\u00b2 | < 12000 \u00b5m\u00b2 |\r\n| Power | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity | Minimized, reported in \u00b5W from simulation activity |\r\n\r\nEach implementation shall have `mkMultBuff` as its top module and shall compile from the complete set of `.sv` files in its source directory, read in any order. `` `include`` directives shall not be used. The targets apply to the results of the open-source flow in Section 7. The slack target leaves margin for physical implementation. Among implementations that meet timing and area, lower area and lower power are preferred.\r\n\r\n## 6. Technology and constraints\r\n\r\nThe open-source flow targets the Nangate45 Open Cell Library, which is built on the FreePDK45 process, at its slowest available corner. The install script written under Section 7 shall obtain the library from a public source, which the report shall identify together with the corner used. The library is not stored in this repository.\r\n\r\nFor comparison with designs built on the GPDK045 library, the sign-off service of Section 8.3 synthesizes the submitted RTL with GPDK045 and simulates the resulting netlists. Its results are reported alongside those of the open-source flow, not in place of them.\r\n\r\n| Constraint | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Clock period | 2.5 ns or 1.25 ns |\r\n| Input delay, all inputs except `clk` | 0 ns |\r\n| Output delay, all outputs | 0 ns |\r\n| Input drive | Output of the smallest D flip-flop in the library |\r\n| Input transition | One eighth of the clock period |\r\n| Output load | Four times the capacitance of one input of the library's X4 two-input NAND (`NAND2_X4` in Nangate45) |\r\n\r\nSynthesis may target a shorter internal clock period and may retime registers. All reported figures are evaluated at the target period.\r\n\r\n## 7. Tool flow\r\n\r\nThe flow shall use open-source tools only and shall be reproducible on a clean Linux host through an install script in the repository. Each step is invoked from the repository root as `make <step> RUN=<400|800>`.\r\n\r\n| Step | Function | Output |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `synth` | Synthesis of `submission/rtl_<RUN>/` to the target library | Netlist and SDF in `submission/outputs/`; reports in `submission/syn_reports/` |\r\n| `check` | RTL simulation with the RTL checker | Simulation log ending in `ALL PASS` |\r\n| `sim` | Gate-level simulation of the netlist with the RTL checker, without back-annotation | Value change dump (VCD) |\r\n| `timing` | Gate-level simulation with SDF back-annotation and the gate-level checker | Simulation log reporting `ALL PASS` or `TIMING FAIL` |\r\n| `power` | Activity-based power analysis from the VCD | Power report |\r\n\r\nOpen-source code and optimization techniques may be used where their licenses permit, with each source cited in the report. Complete implementations of this specification from other sources shall not be used.\r\n\r\n## 8. Verification requirements\r\n\r\nThe harnesses in `starter/tb/` instantiate the design and the memory and generate the clock.\r\n\r\n### 8.1 RTL checker\r\n\r\nThe RTL checker, `submission/testbench/rtl_checker.sv` with top module `mkMultBuff_tb`, shall\r\n\r\n- run at least eight complete fill and drain phases\r\n- drive operands from a random source, in addition to the directed pairs (\u221232768, \u221232768), (\u22121, 1), (0, 32767), (32767, 32767) and (\u22121, \u22121)\r\n- deassert `EN_mult` within a fill phase and `EN_blockRead` within a drain phase\r\n- compare every product returned on `memVal_data` with an independent reference model\r\n- check every observable requirement of Section 4\r\n- print `ALL PASS` if and only if no check has failed\r\n\r\nThe stimulus shall also contain one fill phase with `EN_mult` held at 1 for 64 consecutive cycles and one drain phase with `EN_blockRead` held at 1 for 64 consecutive cycles. These windows are used for power analysis.\r\n\r\n### 8.2 Gate-level checkers\r\n\r\nThe gate-level checkers, `submission/testbench/sdf_checker_400.sv` and `sdf_checker_800.sv` with top modules `mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_400` and `mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_800`, simulate the synthesized netlist with SDF back-annotation at fixed clock periods of 2.5 ns and 1.25 ns. The SDF file is supplied as `+sdf_file=<path>`. Each checker shall\r\n\r\n- drive inputs after the rising edge and sample outputs at the falling edge\r\n- apply random operands over multiple fill and drain phases\r\n- report `TIMING FAIL` for any unknown (X) or incorrect value on `memVal_data` while `VALID_memVal` is 1\r\n- print `ALL PASS` if and only if no failure has occurred\r\n\r\nEach checker shall pass a netlist that meets timing and fail a netlist that violates it. Both outcomes shall be demonstrated and their logs retained. Where the available cell models or simulator do not turn a timing violation into an unknown value, the checker shall detect the violation through the resulting incorrect values, and the report shall describe the limitation.\r\n\r\n### 8.3 Sign-off service\r\n\r\nPushing a branch named `check/<label>` submits the RTL in `submission/rtl_400/` and `submission/rtl_800/` to an independent sign-off service. The latest commit on the branch is checked after each push. The service synthesizes each implementation with GPDK045 under the constraints of Section 6 and simulates the resulting netlists with SDF back-annotation against an independent testbench. Its scorecard is published on branch `check-results`.\r\n\r\n## 9. Deliverables\r\n\r\n```\r\nsubmission/\r\n  rtl_400/       400 MHz implementation\r\n  rtl_800/       800 MHz implementation\r\n  scripts/       synthesis and flow scripts\r\n  testbench/     rtl_checker.sv, sdf_checker_400.sv, sdf_checker_800.sv\r\n  outputs/       synthesis outputs\r\n  syn_reports/   synthesis and power reports\r\n  pdf_report/    report.pdf\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe report shall contain\r\n\r\n1. area and power at both frequencies, as a synthesis estimate and from activity-based analysis\r\n2. the pipeline depth and the critical path at each frequency\r\n3. the changes made to meet 800 MHz\r\n4. a state diagram of every state machine and a datapath diagram showing each pipeline stage and its registers\r\n5. a description of each checker, comparing RTL and gate-level waveforms and identifying effects that appear only at gate level, such as clock-to-output delay and glitches on `RDY_mult`\r\n6. the optimization techniques applied and their measured effect\r\n7. a description of the tool flow and of any departure from the constraints of Section 6\r\n8. a comparison of the open-source results with the GPDK045 sign-off results\r\n9. the external sources used, with citations\r\n10. the source listing, as an appendix\r\n\r\nThe report is generated by the implementing agent and shall be identified as AI-generated on its first page.\r\nCLAUDE.md\r\nMakefile\r\nREADME.md\r\nSPEC.md\r\nbuild\r\ndocs\r\nnotes\r\nstarter\r\nsubmission\r\ntech\r\nbuild:\r\n400\r\nexp\r\nfail_400\r\nfail_800\r\nh.tcl\r\nmutants_400\r\n\r\nsubmission/rtl_400:\r\nmkMultBuff.sv\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\n"]
[1895.521, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat submission/rtl_400/*.sv; cat submission/scripts/synth.tcl submission/scripts/abc_speed.script submission/scripts/resize.tcl; ls build; nproc; uptime\r\n// mkMultBuff.sv -- 400 MHz implementation (2.5 ns clock), Nangate45 slow corner.\r\n//\r\n// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer (SPEC.md).\r\n// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, final adder), with\r\n// // three register ranks (LAT = 3):\r\n//   rank 1: operand register; the multiplier mult_input1 is Booth-recoded\r\n//           before it (one/two/neg digits), the multiplicand is stored as is\r\n//   rank 2: four carry-save rows after partial-product selection and two\r\n//           3:2 levels (9 -> 6 -> 4 rows)\r\n//   rank 3: product, after two more 3:2 levels (4 -> 3 -> 2) and a 32-bit\r\n//           Kogge-Stone adder; drives writeMem_val directly\r\n// Latency (accept -> EN_writeMem) = LAT cycles; a LAT-bit valid shift register\r\n// runs alongside the datapath and drives EN_writeMem (F4).\r\n//\r\n// Control: the two registered ready flags RDY_mult / RDY_blockRead are the\r\n// fill / drain state machine (states FILL = {1,0}, WAIT = {0,0}, DRAIN = {0,1});\r\n// acc_q counts operand pairs accepted in the fill phase, so pairs still in the\r\n// pipeline count against the capacity (F5); ptr_q is the memory address, shared\r\n// by the write pointer (fill) and the read pointer (drain), which never run in\r\n// the same cycle (F13). All outputs come from registers except EN_readMem\r\n// (= EN_blockRead & RDY_blockRead, F7) and memVal_data (= readMem_val, F8).\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (F14, F15).\r\nmodule mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (\r\n    input  logic         clk,\r\n    input  logic         RST_N,\r\n    input  logic         EN_mult,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input0,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input1,\r\n    output logic         RDY_mult,\r\n    input  logic         EN_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         RDY_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         VALID_memVal,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] memVal_data,\r\n    output logic         EN_writeMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   writeMem_addr,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] writeMem_val,\r\n    output logic         EN_readMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   readMem_addr,\r\n    input  logic [N-1:0] readMem_val\r\n);\r\n    // multiplier pipeline configuration (see mult_pipe.sv)\r\n    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b0100;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n                                     + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3] + CPA_SPLIT + 1;\r\n\r\n    logic       rdy_mult_q, rdy_rd_q, vld_q;\r\n    logic [5:0] acc_q, ptr_q;\r\n    logic [LAT-1:0] v_q;                 // valid bit of each pipeline rank\r\n    logic signed [31:0] p;\r\n\r\n    wire acc = EN_mult & rdy_mult_q;\r\n    wire rd  = EN_blockRead & rdy_rd_q;\r\n    wire wr  = v_q[LAT-1];\r\n\r\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n        if (!RST_N) begin\r\n            rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; vld_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            acc_q <= '0; ptr_q <= '0; v_q <= '0;\r\n        end else begin\r\n            v_q <= {v_q[LAT-2:0], acc};\r\n            if (acc) begin\r\n                acc_q <= acc_q + 6'd1;\r\n                if (acc_q == 6'd63) rdy_mult_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            end\r\n            if (wr | rd) ptr_q <= ptr_q + 6'd1;\r\n            if (wr && ptr_q == 6'd63) rdy_rd_q <= 1'b1;\r\n            if (rd && ptr_q == 6'd63) begin\r\n                rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1;\r\n            end\r\n            vld_q <= rd;\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(clk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n\r\n    assign RDY_mult      = rdy_mult_q;\r\n    assign RDY_blockRead = rdy_rd_q;\r\n    assign EN_writeMem   = wr;\r\n    assign writeMem_addr = ptr_q;\r\n    assign writeMem_val  = p;\r\n    assign EN_readMem    = rd;\r\n    assign readMem_addr  = ptr_q;\r\n    assign VALID_memVal  = vld_q;\r\n    assign memVal_data   = readMem_val;\r\nendmodule : mkMultBuff\r\n// mult_pipe.sv -- pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier: radix-4 (modified) Booth\r\n// partial products, carry-save (3:2) reduction 9->6->4->3->2 rows and a final\r\n// carry-propagate adder. Every pipeline cut is optional (parameters), so the\r\n// same source serves the 400 MHz and 800 MHz implementations.\r\n//   PRE_ENC  : Booth-recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n//   ENC_REG  : (PRE_ENC = 0 only) extra rank after the Booth recoding\r\n//   CSA_REG  : bit k set -> register after carry-save level k+1 (k = 0..3)\r\n//   CPA_SPLIT: add the low 16 bits in one stage and the high 16 bits in the next\r\n// Register ranks (= latency from 'en' to 'p'):\r\n//   1 (operand) + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + popcount(CSA_REG) + CPA_SPLIT + 1 (product)\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset. When 'en' is 0 the operand\r\n// register loads zeros (operand isolation), so an idle multiplier does not toggle.\r\n// Written for this project; the Booth recoding and sign-extension constant follow\r\n// the textbook modified-Booth scheme (see the report's references).\r\nmodule mult_pipe #(\r\n    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n    parameter bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1000,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0\r\n) (\r\n    input  logic               clk,\r\n    input  logic               RST_N,\r\n    input  logic               en,     // accept: load operands, else load zeros\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] a,      // multiplicand (unregistered input)\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] b,      // multiplier   (unregistered input)\r\n    output logic signed [31:0] p       // product, registered\r\n);\r\n    // Booth radix-4 recoding of y: digit_i = -2 y[2i+1] + y[2i] + y[2i-1]\r\n    function automatic logic [23:0] booth_enc(input logic [15:0] y);\r\n        logic [16:0] yx;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one, two, neg;\r\n        yx = {y, 1'b0};                       // yx[k+1] = y[k], yx[0] = y[-1] = 0\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin\r\n            one[i] = yx[2*i+1] ^ yx[2*i];\r\n            two[i] = (yx[2*i+2] & ~yx[2*i+1] & ~yx[2*i]) | (~yx[2*i+2] & yx[2*i+1] & yx[2*i]);\r\n            neg[i] = yx[2*i+2];\r\n        end\r\n        booth_enc = {neg, two, one};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ---- stage 0: operand register (operand isolation: zeros when idle)\r\n    logic [7:0]  one_e, two_e, neg_e;\r\n    logic [15:0] a_e;\r\n    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\r\n        // recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_q, two_q, neg_q;\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_q, two_q, neg_q};\r\n    end else begin : g_post\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_d, two_d, neg_d;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {neg_d, two_d, one_d} = booth_enc(b_q);\r\n        if (ENC_REG) begin : g_enc\r\n            logic [7:0]  one_r, two_r, neg_r;\r\n            logic [15:0] a_r;\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n                if (!RST_N) begin a_r <= '0; one_r <= '0; two_r <= '0; neg_r <= '0; end\r\n                else begin a_r <= a_q; one_r <= one_d; two_r <= two_d; neg_r <= neg_d; end\r\n            end\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_r, one_r, two_r, neg_r};\r\n        end else begin : g_noenc\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_d, two_d, neg_d};\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    genvar i;\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // Partial-product rows. Sign extension is replaced by inverting each row's\r\n    // sign bit and adding the constant K = -sum(2^(16+2i)) (mod 2^32); the\r\n    // \"+1\" of each negative row is placed in the free bit of the next row.\r\n    localparam logic [31:0] K = 32'hAAAB_0000;  // -(2^16+2^18+...+2^30) mod 2^32\r\n    wire [16:0] a17 = {a_e[15], a_e};\r\n    wire [16:0] a2  = {a_e, 1'b0};\r\n    logic [31:0] r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8;\r\n    logic [16:0] pp [0:7];\r\n    logic [31:0] rw [0:7];\r\n    generate for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_pp\r\n        assign pp[i] = (({17{one_e[i]}} & a17) | ({17{two_e[i]}} & a2)) ^ {17{neg_e[i]}};\r\n        if (i == 0) begin : g_r0\r\n            assign rw[i] = {15'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0]};\r\n        end else begin : g_ri\r\n            // bits [2i+16:2i] hold the row, bit 2i-2 holds the +1 of row i-1\r\n            assign rw[i] = {13'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0], 1'b0, neg_e[i-1]} << (2*i-2);\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7} = {rw[0], rw[1], rw[2], rw[3], rw[4], rw[5], rw[6], rw[7]};\r\n    assign r8 = K | ({31'd0, neg_e[7]} << 14);\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // carry-save levels (3:2 compressors on whole rows); each optionally registered\r\n    function automatic logic [63:0] csa(input logic [31:0] x, y, z);\r\n        csa = {((x & y) | (x & z) | (y & z)) << 1, x ^ y ^ z};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // level 1: 9 -> 6, level 2: 6 -> 4, level 3: 4 -> 3, level 4: 3 -> 2\r\n    logic [6*32-1:0] l1, l1q;\r\n    logic [4*32-1:0] l2, l2q;\r\n    logic [3*32-1:0] l3, l3q;\r\n    logic [2*32-1:0] l4, l4q;\r\n    assign l1 = {csa(r6, r7, r8), csa(r3, r4, r5), csa(r0, r1, r2)};\r\n    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l4 = csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n\r\n    generate\r\n        if (CSA_REG[0]) begin : g_r1\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l1q <= RST_N ? l1 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n1\r\n            assign l1q = l1;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[1]) begin : g_r2\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l2q <= RST_N ? l2 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n2\r\n            assign l2q = l2;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[2]) begin : g_r3\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l3q <= RST_N ? l3 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n3\r\n            assign l3q = l3;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[3]) begin : g_r4\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l4q <= RST_N ? l4 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n4\r\n            assign l4q = l4;\r\n        end\r\n    endgenerate\r\n    wire [31:0] sx = l4q[31:0], sy = l4q[63:32];\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // final carry-propagate adder, registered product\r\n    generate if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n        logic [16:0] lo;\r\n        logic [15:0] lo_q, xh_q, yh_q;\r\n        logic        c_q;\r\n        assign lo = {1'b0, sx[15:0]} + {1'b0, sy[15:0]};\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                lo_q <= '0; c_q <= 1'b0; xh_q <= '0; yh_q <= '0; p <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                lo_q <= lo[15:0]; c_q <= lo[16];\r\n                xh_q <= sx[31:16]; yh_q <= sy[31:16];\r\n                p    <= {xh_q + yh_q + {15'd0, c_q}, lo_q};\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n    end else begin : g_full\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) p <= '0;\r\n            else        p <= sx + sy;\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\nendmodule : mult_pipe\r\n# synth.tcl -- Yosys synthesis of submission/rtl_$RUN to Nangate45 (slow corner).\r\n# Invoked by the Makefile:  yosys -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl  with env\r\n#   RUN      400 | 800\r\n#   LIB      Liberty file (Nangate45 slow corner)\r\n#   ABC_D    ABC delay target in ps (may be shorter than the clock period)\r\n#   BOOTH    1 to let Yosys build a radix-4 Booth multiplier for '*'\r\n#   OUT      netlist path\r\nyosys -import\r\nset run   $::env(RUN)\r\nset lib   $::env(LIB)\r\nset abc_d $::env(ABC_D)\r\nset booth [expr {[info exists ::env(BOOTH)] ? $::env(BOOTH) : 0}]\r\nset out   $::env(OUT)\r\n# final-adder architecture for $lcu (carry look-ahead unit): a Yosys parallel-prefix choice\r\nset adder [expr {[info exists ::env(ADDER)] ? $::env(ADDER) : \"sklansky\"}]\r\nset extra {}\r\nif {$adder ne \"ripple\"} { set extra [list -extra-map +/choices/${adder}.v] }\r\n\r\nread_liberty -lib $lib\r\n# read every .sv file of the source directory, in any order (SPEC Section 5)\r\nset rtl_dir [expr {[info exists ::env(RTL_DIR)] ? $::env(RTL_DIR) : \"submission/rtl_${run}\"}]\r\nforeach f [lsort [glob ${rtl_dir}/*.sv]] { read_verilog -sv $f }\r\nhierarchy -check -top mkMultBuff\r\nset sargs [list -top mkMultBuff -flatten {*}$extra]\r\nif {$booth} { lappend sargs -booth }\r\nsynth {*}$sargs\r\nopt -full\r\n# sequential mapping: Nangate has no synchronous-reset flop, so the reset is a\r\n# gate in front of D (dfflegalize keeps it synchronous)\r\ndfflibmap -liberty $lib\r\nopt\r\n# ABC: delay-oriented mapping followed by buffering and gate sizing; the\r\n# constraint file gives ABC the input drive and the output load of SPEC Section 6\r\nset cf [open [file rootname $out].abc.constr w]\r\nputs $cf \"set_driving_cell DFF_X1\\nset_load 23.5\"\r\nclose $cf\r\nset abc_script [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_SCRIPT)] ? $::env(ABC_SCRIPT) : \"submission/scripts/abc_speed.script\"}]\r\nif {$abc_script eq \"default\"} {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $lib -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n} else {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $lib -script $abc_script -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n}\r\nfile delete [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\nopt_clean\r\nsetundef -zero\r\nhilomap -singleton -hicell LOGIC1_X1 Z -locell LOGIC0_X1 Z\r\nopt_clean -purge\r\ncheck -assert\r\ntee -o [file rootname $out].stat.rpt stat -liberty $lib\r\nwrite_verilog -noattr -noexpr -nohex -nodec $out\r\n&get -n\r\n&st\r\n&dch\r\n&nf\r\n&st\r\n&syn2\r\n&if -g -K 6\r\n&synch2\r\n&nf\r\n&st\r\n&syn2\r\n&if -g -K 6\r\n&synch2\r\n&nf\r\n&put\r\nbuffer -c\r\ntopo\r\nstime -c\r\nupsize -c\r\ndnsize -c\r\n# resize.tcl -- OpenROAD Resizer on the Yosys netlist: fix slew/capacitance/fanout,\r\n# then gate sizing and buffering for setup and hold.\r\n# Timing inside the Resizer uses the library wire-load model, as the sign-off STA\r\n# does (no parasitics are estimated). A throw-away floorplan and global placement\r\n# are made only because the Resizer needs cell locations to insert buffers\r\n# (without them makeBufferedNet fails and high-fanout nets such as RST_N cannot\r\n# be buffered); the placement is not used for timing and is not an output.\r\n# env: LIB, NETLIST_IN, NETLIST, PERIOD, PDK_LEF_DIR, SETUP_MARGIN\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nset pdk $::env(PDK_LEF_DIR)/..\r\nread_lef $pdk/lef/NangateOpenCellLibrary.tech.lef\r\nread_lef $pdk/lef/NangateOpenCellLibrary.macro.mod.lef\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST_IN)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nsource $pdk/setRC.tcl\r\nset_dont_use {WELLTAP_X1 ANTENNA_X1 FILLCELL_* TBUF_* TINV_* CLKGATE* LOGIC* DLH_* DLL_* TLAT_*}\r\nputs \"== before: [format %.3f [expr {[sta::worst_slack_cmd max] * 1e9}]] ns\"\r\n\r\ninitialize_floorplan -utilization 40 -aspect_ratio 1 -core_space 2 \\\r\n    -site FreePDK45_38x28_10R_NP_162NW_34O\r\nsource $pdk/make_tracks.tcl\r\nplace_pins -hor_layers metal3 -ver_layers metal2 -random\r\nglobal_placement -density 0.6 -skip_io\r\n# timing stays on the wire-load model (no estimate_parasitics)\r\n\r\nset margin [expr {[info exists ::env(SETUP_MARGIN)] ? $::env(SETUP_MARGIN) : 0.15}]\r\nrepair_design\r\nrepair_timing -setup -repair_tns 100 -setup_margin $margin\r\nrepair_timing -hold -hold_margin 0.02\r\nreport_worst_slack -max\r\nreport_worst_slack -min\r\nreport_design_area\r\nwrite_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\n400\r\nexp\r\nfail_400\r\nfail_800\r\nh.tcl\r\nmutants_400\r\n4\r\n 03:05:12 up 35 min,  0 user,  load average: 0.48, 0.73, 0.58\r\n"]
[1896.47, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat Makefile; cat submission/rtl_400/mkMultBuff.sv submission/rtl_400/mult_pipe.sv; ls build/exp build/400\r\n# Makefile -- open-source flow for mkMultBuff (SPEC.md Section 7).\r\n# Usage: make <synth|check|sim|timing|power|all> RUN=<400|800>\r\n# Toolchain: bash submission/scripts/install.sh\r\n\r\nRUN      ?= 400\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 2.5\r\n  HALF    := 1.25\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 2200\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\nelse ifeq ($(RUN),800)\r\n  PERIOD  ?= 1.25\r\n  HALF    := 0.625\r\n  ABC_D   ?= 1050\r\n  BOOTH   ?= 1\r\n  ADDER   ?= kogge-stone\r\nelse\r\n  $(error RUN must be 400 or 800)\r\nendif\r\n\r\nROOT     := $(CURDIR)\r\nLIB      := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary_slow.lib\r\nCELLS    := tech/NangateOpenCellLibrary.v\r\nRTL_DIR  ?= submission/rtl_$(RUN)\r\nRTL      := $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv)\r\nMEM      := starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv starter/rtl/registerArray.sv\r\nTB       := submission/testbench\r\nOUT      := submission/outputs\r\nREP      ?= submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)\r\nBUILD    ?= build/$(RUN)\r\nNETLIST  ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.v\r\nSDF      ?= $(OUT)/mkMultBuff_$(RUN)_map.sdf\r\nSEED     ?= 402\r\nSETUP_MARGIN ?= 0.15\r\n\r\nYOSYS_IMAGE := openroad/orfs@sha256:d3505fd5f930fcd20d3d25a41f3047230b7db7b7797e3448561c9e556cca3774\r\nSTA_IMAGE   := openroad/opensta@sha256:4162b4be70ee69eaa42e5eb3c830433393ff46cf0370f9b6c5b814b48a221a7a\r\nDOCKER      := docker run --rm -v $(ROOT):$(ROOT) -w $(ROOT)\r\nYOSYS       := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e RTL_DIR=$(RTL_DIR) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e ABC_D=$(ABC_D) -e BOOTH=$(BOOTH) -e ADDER=$(ADDER) -e OUT=$(BUILD)/syn.v \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/yosys\r\nOPENROAD    := $(DOCKER) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST_IN=$(BUILD)/syn.v -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               -e SETUP_MARGIN=$(SETUP_MARGIN) -e PDK_LEF_DIR=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/nangate45/lef \\\r\n               $(YOSYS_IMAGE) /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/OpenROAD/bin/openroad -no_init -exit\r\nSTA         := $(DOCKER) -e RUN=$(RUN) -e LIB=$(LIB) -e NETLIST=$(NETLIST) -e SDF=$(SDF) -e PERIOD=$(PERIOD) \\\r\n               --entrypoint /OpenSTA/build/sta $(STA_IMAGE) -no_init -no_splash -exit\r\n\r\n.PHONY: synth check sim timing power all clean timing_fail sta_only\r\n\r\n$(REP) $(BUILD) $(OUT):\r\n\tmkdir -p $@\r\n\r\n# ---- synthesis + static timing (netlist, SDF, area/timing/power-estimate reports)\r\nsynth: | $(REP) $(OUT) $(BUILD)\r\n\t$(YOSYS) -q -l $(REP)/synth.log -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl\r\n\tmv -f $(BUILD)/syn.stat.rpt $(REP)/yosys_area.rpt\r\n\t$(OPENROAD) submission/scripts/resize.tcl > $(REP)/resize.log 2>&1\r\n\t$(STA) submission/scripts/sta.tcl > $(REP)/sta.rpt 2>&1\r\n\tpython3 submission/scripts/sdf_typmax.py $(SDF).sta $(SDF) && rm -f $(SDF).sta\r\n\t@grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns|Total|cell area)\" $(REP)/sta.rpt\r\n\r\n# ---- RTL simulation with the RTL checker\r\ncheck: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=$(HALF) -o $(BUILD)/check.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/rtl_checker.sv $(MEM) $(RTL)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/check.vvp +seed=$(SEED) | tee $(REP)/check.log | tail -25\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/check.log || { echo \"check FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# simulation copy of the netlist: the harness instantiates mkMultBuff #(.N(32)),\r\n# so an (unused) parameter N is declared in the netlist module\r\n$(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v: $(NETLIST) | $(BUILD)\r\n\tsed -e '0,/^module mkMultBuff (/s//module mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (/' $< > $@\r\n\r\n# ---- gate-level simulation (zero delay, no back-annotation) with the RTL checker -> VCD\r\nsim: $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=$(HALF) -o $(BUILD)/sim.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/rtl_checker.sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/sim.vvp +seed=$(SEED) +vcd=$(BUILD)/gate.vcd | tee $(REP)/sim.log | tail -25\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/sim.log || { echo \"sim FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# ---- gate-level simulation with SDF back-annotation and the gate-level checker\r\ntiming: $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tiverilog -g2012 -gspecify -s mkMultBuff_sdf_checker_$(RUN) -o $(BUILD)/timing.vvp \\\r\n\t    $(TB)/sdf_checker_$(RUN).sv $(MEM) $(BUILD)/netlist_sim.v $(CELLS)\r\n\tvvp -n $(BUILD)/timing.vvp +sdf_file=$(SDF) +seed=$(SEED) > $(REP)/timing.log 2>&1 ; true\r\n\t@grep -v -i \"sdf.*warning\" $(REP)/timing.log | tail -12\r\n\t@grep -q \"^ALL PASS\" $(REP)/timing.log || { echo \"timing FAILED\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\n# ---- activity-based power from the gate-level VCD (whole run and the two 64-cycle windows)\r\npower: | $(REP) $(BUILD)\r\n\tbash submission/scripts/power.sh $(REP) $(BUILD) $(NETLIST) $(PERIOD) $(LIB) $(STA_IMAGE)\r\n\r\n# ---- demonstration that the gate-level checker fails a netlist that violates timing\r\n#  RUN=400: the one-stage-multiplier variant in submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage,\r\n#           synthesized with the same flow at 2.5 ns (STA reports negative slack)\r\n#  RUN=800: the 400 MHz netlist, timed by STA and back-annotated at 1.25 ns\r\nFAIL_BUILD := build/fail_$(RUN)\r\nFAIL_REP   := submission/syn_reports/$(RUN)/timing_fail\r\ntiming_fail:\r\n\tmkdir -p $(FAIL_BUILD) $(FAIL_REP)\r\nifeq ($(RUN),400)\r\n\t$(MAKE) synth RUN=400 RTL_DIR=submission/testbench/timing_fail/rtl_onestage BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n\t    NETLIST=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.v SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\nelse\r\n\t$(MAKE) sta_only RUN=800 BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) \\\r\n\t    NETLIST=$(OUT)/mkMultBuff_400_map.v SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\nendif\r\n\t-$(MAKE) timing RUN=$(RUN) BUILD=$(FAIL_BUILD) REP=$(FAIL_REP) NETLIST=$(if $(filter 400,$(RUN)),$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.v,$(OUT)/mkMultBuff_400_map.v) SDF=$(FAIL_BUILD)/fail_map.sdf\r\n\t@grep -q \"TIMING FAIL\" $(FAIL_REP)/timing.log && echo \"timing_fail: checker reported TIMING FAIL as expected\" \\\r\n\t    || { echo \"timing_fail: checker did NOT fail\"; exit 1; }\r\n\r\nsta_only: | $(REP)\r\n\t$(STA) submission/scripts/sta.tcl > $(REP)/sta.rpt 2>&1\r\n\tpython3 submission/scripts/sdf_typmax.py $(SDF).sta $(SDF) && rm -f $(SDF).sta\r\n\t@grep -E \"^(worst slack|tns)\" $(REP)/sta.rpt\r\n\r\nall: synth check sim timing power\r\n\r\nclean:\r\n\trm -rf build\r\n// mkMultBuff.sv -- 400 MHz implementation (2.5 ns clock), Nangate45 slow corner.\r\n//\r\n// Pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier with a 64-entry fill/drain buffer (SPEC.md).\r\n// Datapath: mult_pipe (radix-4 Booth, carry-save reduction, final adder), with\r\n// // three register ranks (LAT = 3):\r\n//   rank 1: operand register; the multiplier mult_input1 is Booth-recoded\r\n//           before it (one/two/neg digits), the multiplicand is stored as is\r\n//   rank 2: four carry-save rows after partial-product selection and two\r\n//           3:2 levels (9 -> 6 -> 4 rows)\r\n//   rank 3: product, after two more 3:2 levels (4 -> 3 -> 2) and a 32-bit\r\n//           Kogge-Stone adder; drives writeMem_val directly\r\n// Latency (accept -> EN_writeMem) = LAT cycles; a LAT-bit valid shift register\r\n// runs alongside the datapath and drives EN_writeMem (F4).\r\n//\r\n// Control: the two registered ready flags RDY_mult / RDY_blockRead are the\r\n// fill / drain state machine (states FILL = {1,0}, WAIT = {0,0}, DRAIN = {0,1});\r\n// acc_q counts operand pairs accepted in the fill phase, so pairs still in the\r\n// pipeline count against the capacity (F5); ptr_q is the memory address, shared\r\n// by the write pointer (fill) and the read pointer (drain), which never run in\r\n// the same cycle (F13). All outputs come from registers except EN_readMem\r\n// (= EN_blockRead & RDY_blockRead, F7) and memVal_data (= readMem_val, F8).\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset (F14, F15).\r\nmodule mkMultBuff #(parameter N = 32) (\r\n    input  logic         clk,\r\n    input  logic         RST_N,\r\n    input  logic         EN_mult,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input0,\r\n    input  logic [15:0]  mult_input1,\r\n    output logic         RDY_mult,\r\n    input  logic         EN_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         RDY_blockRead,\r\n    output logic         VALID_memVal,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] memVal_data,\r\n    output logic         EN_writeMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   writeMem_addr,\r\n    output logic [N-1:0] writeMem_val,\r\n    output logic         EN_readMem,\r\n    output logic [5:0]   readMem_addr,\r\n    input  logic [N-1:0] readMem_val\r\n);\r\n    // multiplier pipeline configuration (see mult_pipe.sv)\r\n    localparam bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1;\r\n    localparam bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b0100;\r\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0;\r\n    localparam int       LAT       = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1]\r\n                                     + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3] + CPA_SPLIT + 1;\r\n\r\n    logic       rdy_mult_q, rdy_rd_q, vld_q;\r\n    logic [5:0] acc_q, ptr_q;\r\n    logic [LAT-1:0] v_q;                 // valid bit of each pipeline rank\r\n    logic signed [31:0] p;\r\n\r\n    wire acc = EN_mult & rdy_mult_q;\r\n    wire rd  = EN_blockRead & rdy_rd_q;\r\n    wire wr  = v_q[LAT-1];\r\n\r\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n        if (!RST_N) begin\r\n            rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1; rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; vld_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            acc_q <= '0; ptr_q <= '0; v_q <= '0;\r\n        end else begin\r\n            v_q <= {v_q[LAT-2:0], acc};\r\n            if (acc) begin\r\n                acc_q <= acc_q + 6'd1;\r\n                if (acc_q == 6'd63) rdy_mult_q <= 1'b0;\r\n            end\r\n            if (wr | rd) ptr_q <= ptr_q + 6'd1;\r\n            if (wr && ptr_q == 6'd63) rdy_rd_q <= 1'b1;\r\n            if (rd && ptr_q == 6'd63) begin\r\n                rdy_rd_q <= 1'b0; rdy_mult_q <= 1'b1;\r\n            end\r\n            vld_q <= rd;\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\n\r\n    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\r\n        u_mult (.clk(clk), .RST_N(RST_N), .en(acc), .a(mult_input0), .b(mult_input1), .p(p));\r\n\r\n    assign RDY_mult      = rdy_mult_q;\r\n    assign RDY_blockRead = rdy_rd_q;\r\n    assign EN_writeMem   = wr;\r\n    assign writeMem_addr = ptr_q;\r\n    assign writeMem_val  = p;\r\n    assign EN_readMem    = rd;\r\n    assign readMem_addr  = ptr_q;\r\n    assign VALID_memVal  = vld_q;\r\n    assign memVal_data   = readMem_val;\r\nendmodule : mkMultBuff\r\n// mult_pipe.sv -- pipelined signed 16x16 multiplier: radix-4 (modified) Booth\r\n// partial products, carry-save (3:2) reduction 9->6->4->3->2 rows and a final\r\n// carry-propagate adder. Every pipeline cut is optional (parameters), so the\r\n// same source serves the 400 MHz and 800 MHz implementations.\r\n//   PRE_ENC  : Booth-recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n//   ENC_REG  : (PRE_ENC = 0 only) extra rank after the Booth recoding\r\n//   CSA_REG  : bit k set -> register after carry-save level k+1 (k = 0..3)\r\n//   CPA_SPLIT: add the low 16 bits in one stage and the high 16 bits in the next\r\n// Register ranks (= latency from 'en' to 'p'):\r\n//   1 (operand) + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + popcount(CSA_REG) + CPA_SPLIT + 1 (product)\r\n// Every register has a synchronous active-low reset. When 'en' is 0 the operand\r\n// register loads zeros (operand isolation), so an idle multiplier does not toggle.\r\n// Written for this project; the Booth recoding and sign-extension constant follow\r\n// the textbook modified-Booth scheme (see the report's references).\r\nmodule mult_pipe #(\r\n    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n    parameter bit       ENC_REG   = 1'b0,\r\n    parameter bit [3:0] CSA_REG   = 4'b1000,\r\n    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0\r\n) (\r\n    input  logic               clk,\r\n    input  logic               RST_N,\r\n    input  logic               en,     // accept: load operands, else load zeros\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] a,      // multiplicand (unregistered input)\r\n    input  logic signed [15:0] b,      // multiplier   (unregistered input)\r\n    output logic signed [31:0] p       // product, registered\r\n);\r\n    // Booth radix-4 recoding of y: digit_i = -2 y[2i+1] + y[2i] + y[2i-1]\r\n    function automatic logic [23:0] booth_enc(input logic [15:0] y);\r\n        logic [16:0] yx;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one, two, neg;\r\n        yx = {y, 1'b0};                       // yx[k+1] = y[k], yx[0] = y[-1] = 0\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin\r\n            one[i] = yx[2*i+1] ^ yx[2*i];\r\n            two[i] = (yx[2*i+2] & ~yx[2*i+1] & ~yx[2*i]) | (~yx[2*i+2] & yx[2*i+1] & yx[2*i]);\r\n            neg[i] = yx[2*i+2];\r\n        end\r\n        booth_enc = {neg, two, one};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // ---- stage 0: operand register (operand isolation: zeros when idle)\r\n    logic [7:0]  one_e, two_e, neg_e;\r\n    logic [15:0] a_e;\r\n    generate if (PRE_ENC) begin : g_pre\r\n        // recode the multiplier before the operand register\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_q, two_q, neg_q;\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin\r\n                a_q <= '0; one_q <= '0; two_q <= '0; neg_q <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                a_q <= a; {neg_q, two_q, one_q} <= booth_enc(b);\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_q, two_q, neg_q};\r\n    end else begin : g_post\r\n        logic [15:0] a_q, b_q;\r\n        logic [7:0]  one_d, two_d, neg_d;\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N || !en) begin a_q <= '0; b_q <= '0; end\r\n            else               begin a_q <= a;  b_q <= b;  end\r\n        end\r\n        assign {neg_d, two_d, one_d} = booth_enc(b_q);\r\n        if (ENC_REG) begin : g_enc\r\n            logic [7:0]  one_r, two_r, neg_r;\r\n            logic [15:0] a_r;\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n                if (!RST_N) begin a_r <= '0; one_r <= '0; two_r <= '0; neg_r <= '0; end\r\n                else begin a_r <= a_q; one_r <= one_d; two_r <= two_d; neg_r <= neg_d; end\r\n            end\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_r, one_r, two_r, neg_r};\r\n        end else begin : g_noenc\r\n            assign {a_e, one_e, two_e, neg_e} = {a_q, one_d, two_d, neg_d};\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    genvar i;\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // Partial-product rows. Sign extension is replaced by inverting each row's\r\n    // sign bit and adding the constant K = -sum(2^(16+2i)) (mod 2^32); the\r\n    // \"+1\" of each negative row is placed in the free bit of the next row.\r\n    localparam logic [31:0] K = 32'hAAAB_0000;  // -(2^16+2^18+...+2^30) mod 2^32\r\n    wire [16:0] a17 = {a_e[15], a_e};\r\n    wire [16:0] a2  = {a_e, 1'b0};\r\n    logic [31:0] r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8;\r\n    logic [16:0] pp [0:7];\r\n    logic [31:0] rw [0:7];\r\n    generate for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_pp\r\n        assign pp[i] = (({17{one_e[i]}} & a17) | ({17{two_e[i]}} & a2)) ^ {17{neg_e[i]}};\r\n        if (i == 0) begin : g_r0\r\n            assign rw[i] = {15'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0]};\r\n        end else begin : g_ri\r\n            // bits [2i+16:2i] hold the row, bit 2i-2 holds the +1 of row i-1\r\n            assign rw[i] = {13'd0, ~pp[i][16], pp[i][15:0], 1'b0, neg_e[i-1]} << (2*i-2);\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7} = {rw[0], rw[1], rw[2], rw[3], rw[4], rw[5], rw[6], rw[7]};\r\n    assign r8 = K | ({31'd0, neg_e[7]} << 14);\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // carry-save levels (3:2 compressors on whole rows); each optionally registered\r\n    function automatic logic [63:0] csa(input logic [31:0] x, y, z);\r\n        csa = {((x & y) | (x & z) | (y & z)) << 1, x ^ y ^ z};\r\n    endfunction\r\n\r\n    // level 1: 9 -> 6, level 2: 6 -> 4, level 3: 4 -> 3, level 4: 3 -> 2\r\n    logic [6*32-1:0] l1, l1q;\r\n    logic [4*32-1:0] l2, l2q;\r\n    logic [3*32-1:0] l3, l3q;\r\n    logic [2*32-1:0] l4, l4q;\r\n    assign l1 = {csa(r6, r7, r8), csa(r3, r4, r5), csa(r0, r1, r2)};\r\n    assign l2 = {csa(l1q[3*32 +: 32], l1q[4*32 +: 32], l1q[5*32 +: 32]),\r\n                 csa(l1q[0*32 +: 32], l1q[1*32 +: 32], l1q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l3 = {l2q[3*32 +: 32], csa(l2q[0*32 +: 32], l2q[1*32 +: 32], l2q[2*32 +: 32])};\r\n    assign l4 = csa(l3q[0*32 +: 32], l3q[1*32 +: 32], l3q[2*32 +: 32]);\r\n\r\n    generate\r\n        if (CSA_REG[0]) begin : g_r1\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l1q <= RST_N ? l1 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n1\r\n            assign l1q = l1;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[1]) begin : g_r2\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l2q <= RST_N ? l2 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n2\r\n            assign l2q = l2;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[2]) begin : g_r3\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l3q <= RST_N ? l3 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n3\r\n            assign l3q = l3;\r\n        end\r\n        if (CSA_REG[3]) begin : g_r4\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) l4q <= RST_N ? l4 : '0;\r\n        end else begin : g_n4\r\n            assign l4q = l4;\r\n        end\r\n    endgenerate\r\n    wire [31:0] sx = l4q[31:0], sy = l4q[63:32];\r\n\r\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // final carry-propagate adder, registered product\r\n    generate if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n        logic [16:0] lo;\r\n        logic [15:0] lo_q, xh_q, yh_q;\r\n        logic        c_q;\r\n        assign lo = {1'b0, sx[15:0]} + {1'b0, sy[15:0]};\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                lo_q <= '0; c_q <= 1'b0; xh_q <= '0; yh_q <= '0; p <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                lo_q <= lo[15:0]; c_q <= lo[16];\r\n                xh_q <= sx[31:16]; yh_q <= sy[31:16];\r\n                p    <= {xh_q + yh_q + {15'd0, c_q}, lo_q};\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n    end else begin : g_full\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) p <= '0;\r\n            else        p <= sx + sy;\r\n        end\r\n    end endgenerate\r\nendmodule : mult_pipe\r\nbuild/400:\r\ncheck.vvp\r\ngate.vcd\r\nnetlist_sim.v\r\nsim.vvp\r\nsyn.v\r\ntiming.vvp\r\n\r\nbuild/exp:\r\nabc_p.script\r\ne800a\r\ne800b\r\ne800c\r\nf400\r\nf800b\r\nft\r\ng400\r\ng800b\r\nm.vvp\r\nmult_pipe.sv\r\np400a\r\np400b\r\np400c\r\npath.sh\r\nq400a\r\nq400b\r\nq400c\r\nq400d\r\nr400_1500\r\nr400_1800\r\nr400_2300\r\nrsz.tcl\r\nrsz.v\r\nrun.sh\r\ns400a\r\ns400b\r\ns400c\r\nt2.vvp\r\nt400a\r\nt400b\r\nt400c\r\nt400d\r\ntb2.sv\r\ntb_mult.sv\r\ntop.sv\r\nu400a\r\nu400b\r\n"]
[1899.386, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat submission/scripts/synth.tcl submission/scripts/resize.tcl submission/scripts/abc_speed.script; cat submission/scripts/constraints.tcl; head -60 submission/scripts/sta.tcl\r\n# synth.tcl -- Yosys synthesis of submission/rtl_$RUN to Nangate45 (slow corner).\r\n# Invoked by the Makefile:  yosys -c submission/scripts/synth.tcl  with env\r\n#   RUN      400 | 800\r\n#   LIB      Liberty file (Nangate45 slow corner)\r\n#   ABC_D    ABC delay target in ps (may be shorter than the clock period)\r\n#   BOOTH    1 to let Yosys build a radix-4 Booth multiplier for '*'\r\n#   OUT      netlist path\r\nyosys -import\r\nset run   $::env(RUN)\r\nset lib   $::env(LIB)\r\nset abc_d $::env(ABC_D)\r\nset booth [expr {[info exists ::env(BOOTH)] ? $::env(BOOTH) : 0}]\r\nset out   $::env(OUT)\r\n# final-adder architecture for $lcu (carry look-ahead unit): a Yosys parallel-prefix choice\r\nset adder [expr {[info exists ::env(ADDER)] ? $::env(ADDER) : \"sklansky\"}]\r\nset extra {}\r\nif {$adder ne \"ripple\"} { set extra [list -extra-map +/choices/${adder}.v] }\r\n\r\nread_liberty -lib $lib\r\n# read every .sv file of the source directory, in any order (SPEC Section 5)\r\nset rtl_dir [expr {[info exists ::env(RTL_DIR)] ? $::env(RTL_DIR) : \"submission/rtl_${run}\"}]\r\nforeach f [lsort [glob ${rtl_dir}/*.sv]] { read_verilog -sv $f }\r\nhierarchy -check -top mkMultBuff\r\nset sargs [list -top mkMultBuff -flatten {*}$extra]\r\nif {$booth} { lappend sargs -booth }\r\nsynth {*}$sargs\r\nopt -full\r\n# sequential mapping: Nangate has no synchronous-reset flop, so the reset is a\r\n# gate in front of D (dfflegalize keeps it synchronous)\r\ndfflibmap -liberty $lib\r\nopt\r\n# ABC: delay-oriented mapping followed by buffering and gate sizing; the\r\n# constraint file gives ABC the input drive and the output load of SPEC Section 6\r\nset cf [open [file rootname $out].abc.constr w]\r\nputs $cf \"set_driving_cell DFF_X1\\nset_load 23.5\"\r\nclose $cf\r\nset abc_script [expr {[info exists ::env(ABC_SCRIPT)] ? $::env(ABC_SCRIPT) : \"submission/scripts/abc_speed.script\"}]\r\nif {$abc_script eq \"default\"} {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $lib -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n} else {\r\n    abc -D $abc_d -liberty $lib -script $abc_script -constr [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\n}\r\nfile delete [file rootname $out].abc.constr\r\nopt_clean\r\nsetundef -zero\r\nhilomap -singleton -hicell LOGIC1_X1 Z -locell LOGIC0_X1 Z\r\nopt_clean -purge\r\ncheck -assert\r\ntee -o [file rootname $out].stat.rpt stat -liberty $lib\r\nwrite_verilog -noattr -noexpr -nohex -nodec $out\r\n# resize.tcl -- OpenROAD Resizer on the Yosys netlist: fix slew/capacitance/fanout,\r\n# then gate sizing and buffering for setup and hold.\r\n# Timing inside the Resizer uses the library wire-load model, as the sign-off STA\r\n# does (no parasitics are estimated). A throw-away floorplan and global placement\r\n# are made only because the Resizer needs cell locations to insert buffers\r\n# (without them makeBufferedNet fails and high-fanout nets such as RST_N cannot\r\n# be buffered); the placement is not used for timing and is not an output.\r\n# env: LIB, NETLIST_IN, NETLIST, PERIOD, PDK_LEF_DIR, SETUP_MARGIN\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nset pdk $::env(PDK_LEF_DIR)/..\r\nread_lef $pdk/lef/NangateOpenCellLibrary.tech.lef\r\nread_lef $pdk/lef/NangateOpenCellLibrary.macro.mod.lef\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST_IN)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nsource $pdk/setRC.tcl\r\nset_dont_use {WELLTAP_X1 ANTENNA_X1 FILLCELL_* TBUF_* TINV_* CLKGATE* LOGIC* DLH_* DLL_* TLAT_*}\r\nputs \"== before: [format %.3f [expr {[sta::worst_slack_cmd max] * 1e9}]] ns\"\r\n\r\ninitialize_floorplan -utilization 40 -aspect_ratio 1 -core_space 2 \\\r\n    -site FreePDK45_38x28_10R_NP_162NW_34O\r\nsource $pdk/make_tracks.tcl\r\nplace_pins -hor_layers metal3 -ver_layers metal2 -random\r\nglobal_placement -density 0.6 -skip_io\r\n# timing stays on the wire-load model (no estimate_parasitics)\r\n\r\nset margin [expr {[info exists ::env(SETUP_MARGIN)] ? $::env(SETUP_MARGIN) : 0.15}]\r\nrepair_design\r\nrepair_timing -setup -repair_tns 100 -setup_margin $margin\r\nrepair_timing -hold -hold_margin 0.02\r\nreport_worst_slack -max\r\nreport_worst_slack -min\r\nreport_design_area\r\nwrite_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\n&get -n\r\n&st\r\n&dch\r\n&nf\r\n&st\r\n&syn2\r\n&if -g -K 6\r\n&synch2\r\n&nf\r\n&st\r\n&syn2\r\n&if -g -K 6\r\n&synch2\r\n&nf\r\n&put\r\nbuffer -c\r\ntopo\r\nstime -c\r\nupsize -c\r\ndnsize -c\r\n# constraints.tcl -- SPEC.md Section 6 constraints for OpenSTA. Needs $period (ns).\r\nset clk_port [get_ports clk]\r\ncreate_clock -name clk -period $period $clk_port\r\nset_clock_transition [expr {$period / 8.0}] [get_clocks clk]\r\nset in_ports [lsearch -inline -all -not -exact [all_inputs] $clk_port]\r\nset_input_delay  0.0 -clock clk $in_ports\r\nset_output_delay 0.0 -clock clk [all_outputs]\r\n# input drive: output of the smallest D flip-flop (DFF_X1/Q), whose clock input\r\n# has a transition of one eighth of the clock period\r\nset_driving_cell -lib_cell DFF_X1 -pin Q -from_pin CK \\\r\n    -input_transition_rise [expr {$period / 8.0}] \\\r\n    -input_transition_fall [expr {$period / 8.0}] $in_ports\r\n# output load: 4 x input capacitance of NAND2_X4 (pin A1)\r\nset c_nand [get_property [get_lib_pins */NAND2_X4/A1] capacitance]\r\nset_load [expr {4.0 * $c_nand}] [all_outputs]\r\n# pre-layout wire estimate: the library's default wire-load model\r\nset_wire_load_model -name 5K_hvratio_1_1\r\n# sta.tcl -- OpenSTA timing at the target period; writes the SDF for gate-level sim.\r\n# env: RUN, LIB, NETLIST, SDF, PERIOD (ns)\r\nset period $::env(PERIOD)\r\nread_liberty $::env(LIB)\r\nread_verilog $::env(NETLIST)\r\nlink_design mkMultBuff\r\nsource submission/scripts/constraints.tcl\r\nputs \"== constraints: period $period ns, clock/input transition [expr {$period/8.0}] ns, output load [expr {4.0*$c_nand}] fF\"\r\nreport_checks -path_delay max -group_path_count 3 -format full_clock_expanded \\\r\n    -fields {slew cap input_pins fanout} -digits 3\r\nreport_checks -path_delay min -format full_clock_expanded -fields {slew cap input_pins} -digits 3\r\nputs \"== summary\"\r\nreport_worst_slack -max -digits 3\r\nreport_worst_slack -min -digits 3\r\nreport_tns -digits 3\r\nreport_check_types -max_slew -max_capacitance -max_fanout -violators\r\nreport_power -digits 4\r\n# cell area of the final netlist, from the Liberty areas\r\nset area 0.0\r\narray set hist {}\r\nforeach inst [get_cells *] {\r\n    set lc [get_property $inst ref_name]\r\n    set a [get_property [get_lib_cells */$lc] area]\r\n    set area [expr {$area + $a}]\r\n    if {[info exists hist($lc)]} { incr hist($lc) } else { set hist($lc) 1 }\r\n}\r\nset seq 0.0\r\nforeach lc [lsort [array names hist]] {\r\n    set a [get_property [get_lib_cells */$lc] area]\r\n    if {[string match DFF* $lc]} { set seq [expr {$seq + $a * $hist($lc)}] }\r\n    puts [format \"cell %-14s %5d  %9.3f um^2\" $lc $hist($lc) [expr {$a * $hist($lc)}]]\r\n}\r\nputs [format \"cell area %.3f um^2 (sequential %.3f um^2, %d instances)\" $area $seq [llength [get_cells *]]]\r\nwrite_sdf -include_typ -digits 4 -no_timestamp $::env(SDF).sta\r\nputs \"SDF written to $::env(SDF)\"\r\n"]
[1929.748, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m PRE=1 build/exp/run.sh h800a 1.25 0 1111 1 1000 0 kogge-stone 2>&1 | grep -v Warning; build/exp/path.sh build/exp/h800a/sta.rpt | head -30; grep -A40 \"^Startpoint\" build/exp/h800a/sta.rpt | grep -m3 -E \"Startpoint|Endpoint\"\r\nh800a P=1.25 enc=0 csa=1111 spl=1 abcD=1000 | yosys_area=4100.390000 rsz_area=5025 wns=-0.764 whs=0.028 pwr_est=2.5588e-03\r\nby clk) fo=Startpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\nby clk) fo=Endpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\n_4132_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=6 d=0.473 t=0.473\r\n_2202_/ZN (OAI221_X2) fo=1 d=0.128 t=0.601\r\n_2205_/ZN (AOI211_X2) fo=1 d=0.237 t=0.838\r\n_2212_/ZN (OAI21_X1) fo=3 d=0.107 t=0.946\r\n_2249_/ZN (AND3_X2) fo=1 d=0.111 t=1.057\r\n_2260_/ZN (AOI211_X2) fo=2 d=0.306 t=1.362\r\n_2276_/ZN (AOI221_X2) fo=1 d=0.124 t=1.486\r\n_2278_/ZN (NOR3_X4) fo=1 d=0.119 t=1.605\r\n_2279_/Z (MUX2_X1) fo=1 d=0.239 t=1.845\r\n_2280_/Z (BUF_X4) fo=1 d=0.082 t=1.927\r\n                                     1.927   data arrival time\r\n                           -0.087    1.163   library setup time\r\n                                    -1.927   data arrival time\r\nslack (VIOLATED) fo=-0.764 d= t=\r\nStartpoint: _4132_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nEndpoint: _4185_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\nStartpoint: _4131_ (rising edge-triggered flip-flop clocked by clk)\r\n"]
[1933.326, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m for d in e800a f800b g800b; do grep -E \"^(worst slack|cell area)\" build/exp/$d/sta.rpt; done; bash build/exp/path.sh build/exp/g800b/sta.rpt | head -40\r\nworst slack max -2.760\r\nworst slack min 0.026\r\ncell area 4235.784 um^2 (sequential 2193.170 um^2, 2126 instances)\r\nworst slack max -1.136\r\nworst slack min 0.026\r\ncell area 3654.574 um^2 (sequential 1510.348 um^2, 1766 instances)\r\nworst slack max -0.729\r\nworst slack min 0.028\r\ncell area 4181.520 um^2 (sequential 1537.480 um^2, 1838 instances)\r\nby clk) fo=Startpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\nby clk) fo=Endpoint: d=edge-triggered t=flip-flop\r\n_3202_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=5 d=0.459 t=0.459\r\n_2059_/Z (XOR2_X2) fo=2 d=0.211 t=0.670\r\n_2060_/ZN (AND2_X2) fo=1 d=0.117 t=0.788\r\n_2061_/ZN (AOI222_X2) fo=2 d=0.059 t=0.847\r\n_2065_/ZN (AOI221_X2) fo=2 d=0.394 t=1.241\r\n_2099_/ZN (OAI21_X2) fo=3 d=0.129 t=1.370\r\n_2100_/ZN (NAND2_X2) fo=2 d=0.100 t=1.470\r\n_2101_/ZN (OAI22_X1) fo=2 d=0.074 t=1.544\r\n_2105_/ZN (OR3_X4) fo=1 d=0.278 t=1.822\r\n_2106_/ZN (AOI21_X4) fo=1 d=0.097 t=1.919\r\n                                     1.919   data arrival time\r\n                           -0.060    1.190   library setup time\r\n                                    -1.919   data arrival time\r\nslack (VIOLATED) fo=-0.729 d= t=\r\n"]
[1966.353, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m grep -n \"PRE_ENC   = \\|CPA_SPLIT = \\|assign r8\\|assign l1 = \\|wire \\[31:0\\] sx\\|generate if (CPA_SPLIT)\\|end else begin : g_full\\|end endgenerate\\|endmodule\" build/exp/mult_pipe.sv\r\n10:    parameter bit       PRE_ENC   = 1'b1,\r\n13:    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0\r\n69:    end endgenerate\r\n90:    end endgenerate\r\n92:    assign r8 = K | ({31'd0, neg_e[7]} << 14);\r\n105:    assign l1 = {csa(r6, r7, r8), csa(r3, r4, r5), csa(r0, r1, r2)};\r\n133:    wire [31:0] sx = l4q[31:0], sy = l4q[63:32];\r\n137:    generate if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\r\n151:    end else begin : g_full\r\n156:    end endgenerate\r\n157:endmodule : mult_pipe\r\n"]
[1978.702, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m IMG=openroad/orfs@sha256:d3505fd5f930fcd20d3d25a41f3047230b7db7b7797e3448561c9e556cca3774; docker run --rm $IMG bash -c 'A=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/yosys-abc; ls /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/; $A -c \"retime -h; dretime -h; lcorr -h\" 2>&1 | head -80; /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/tools/install/yosys/bin/yosys -p \"help synth\" | grep -n -i -B1 -A2 \"retime\\|booth\"; grep -rn retime /OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/scripts/*.tcl | head'\r\nyosys\r\nyosys-abc\r\nyosys-config\r\nyosys-filterlib\r\nyosys-smtbmc\r\nyosys-witness\r\n======== ABC command line \"retime -h; dretime -h; lcorr -h\"\r\nusage: retime [-MD num] [-fbsovh]\r\n\t         retimes the current network using one of the algorithms:\r\n\t             1: most forward retiming\r\n\t             2: most backward retiming\r\n\t             3: forward and backward min-area retiming\r\n\t             4: forward and backward min-delay retiming\r\n\t             5: mode 3 followed by mode 4\r\n\t             6: Pan's optimum-delay retiming using binary search\r\n\t-M num : the retiming algorithm to use [default = 5]\r\n\t-D num : the minimum delay target (0=unused) [default = 0]\r\n\t-f     : enables forward-only retiming in modes 3,4,5 [default = no]\r\n\t-b     : enables backward-only retiming in modes 3,4,5 [default = no]\r\n\t-s     : enables retiming one step only in mode 4 [default = no]\r\n\t-o     : enables usind old flop naming conventions [default = no]\r\n\t-v     : enables verbose output [default = no]\r\n\t-h     : print the command usage\r\n42-\r\n43:    -booth\r\n44:        run the booth pass to map $mul to Booth encoded multipliers\r\n45-\r\n46-    -arith_tree\r\n--\r\n103-        techmap -map +/cmp2lut.v -map +/cmp2lcu.v     (if -lut)\r\n104:        booth        (if -booth)\r\n105-        alumacc      (unless -noalumacc)\r\n106-        arith_tree     (if -arith_tree)\r\n/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/scripts/synth.tcl:197:  abc -dff -script $::env(SCRIPTS_DIR)/abc_retime.script\r\n"]
[1989.923, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m python3 - <<'EOF'\r\np='build/exp/mult_pipe.sv'\r\ns=open(p).read()\r\ns=s.replace(\"    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0\\n\",\"    parameter bit       SEL_REG   = 1'b0,\\n    parameter bit       CPA_SPLIT = 1'b0,\\n    parameter bit       CPA_CSEL  = 1'b0\\n\")\r\ns=s.replace(\"assign l1 = {csa(r6, r7, r8), csa(r3, r4, r5), csa(r0, r1, r2)};\",\r\n\"\"\"// optional register after partial-product selection (8 rows of 17 bits + the\r\n    // row +1 bits; the constant part of row 8 is re-created after the register)\r\n    logic [31:0] q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8;\r\n    generate if (SEL_REG) begin : g_sel\r\n        logic [16:0] ppq [0:7];\r\n        logic [7:0]  negq;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) begin : g_q\r\n            always_ff @(posedge clk) ppq[i] <= RST_N ? pp[i] : 17'd0;\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) negq <= RST_N ? neg_e : 8'd0;\r\n        assign q0 = {15'd0, ~ppq[0][16], ppq[0][15:0]};\r\n        assign q1 = {13'd0, ~ppq[1][16], ppq[1][15:0], 1'b0, negq[0]} << 0;\r\n        assign q2 = {13'd0, ~ppq[2][16], ppq[2][15:0], 1'b0, negq[1]} << 2;\r\n        assign q3 = {13'd0, ~ppq[3][16], ppq[3][15:0], 1'b0, negq[2]} << 4;\r\n        assign q4 = {13'd0, ~ppq[4][16], ppq[4][15:0], 1'b0, negq[3]} << 6;\r\n        assign q5 = {13'd0, ~ppq[5][16], ppq[5][15:0], 1'b0, negq[4]} << 8;\r\n        assign q6 = {13'd0, ~ppq[6][16], ppq[6][15:0], 1'b0, negq[5]} << 10;\r\n        assign q7 = {13'd0, ~ppq[7][16], ppq[7][15:0], 1'b0, negq[6]} << 12;\r\n        assign q8 = K | ({31'd0, negq[7]} << 14);\r\n    end else begin : g_nosel\r\n        assign {q0, q1, q2, q3, q4, q5, q6, q7, q8} = {r0, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8};\r\n    end endgenerate\r\n    assign l1 = {csa(q6, q7, q8), csa(q3, q4, q5), csa(q0, q1, q2)};\"\"\")\r\nold=s[s.index(\"    generate if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\"):s.index(\"endmodule\")]\r\nnew=\"\"\"    generate if (CPA_CSEL) begin : g_csel\r\n        // two-stage carry-select adder: stage A adds each 8-bit block with\r\n        // carry-in 0 and 1; stage B resolves the block carries and selects\r\n        logic [8:0]  s0 [0:3], s1 [1:3];\r\n        logic [7:0]  s0q [0:3], s1q [1:3];\r\n        logic [2:0]  c0q;\r\n        logic [2:1]  c1q;\r\n        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) begin : g_blk\r\n            assign s0[i] = {1'b0, sx[8*i +: 8]} + {1'b0, sy[8*i +: 8]};\r\n            if (i > 0) begin : g_one\r\n                assign s1[i] = {1'b0, sx[8*i +: 8]} + {1'b0, sy[8*i +: 8]} + 9'd1;\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\r\n            if (!RST_N) begin\r\n                s0q[0] <= '0; s0q[1] <= '0; s0q[2] <= '0; s0q[3] <= '0;\r\n                s1q[1] <= '0; s1q[2] <= '0; s1q[3] <= '0;\r\n                c0q <= '0; c1q <= '0; p <= '0;\r\n            end else begin\r\n                s0q[0] <= s0[0][7:0]; s0q[1] <= s0[1][7:0]; s0q[2] <= s0[2][7:0]; s0q[3] <= s0[3][7:0];\r\n                s1q[1] <= s1[1][7:0]; s1q[2] <= s1[2][7:0]; s1q[3] <= s1[3][7:0];\r\n                c0q <= {s0[2][8], s0[1][8], s0[0][8]};\r\n                c1q <= {s1[2][8], s1[1][8]};\r\n                p   <= {cin3 ? s1q[3] : s0q[3], cin2 ? s1q[2] : s0q[2],\r\n                        cin1 ? s1q[1] : s0q[1], s0q[0]};\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n        wire cin1 = c0q[0];\r\n        wire cin2 = c0q[1] | (c1q[1] & cin1);\r\n        wire cin3 = c0q[2] | (c1q[2] & cin2);\r\n\"\"\"+old.replace(\"    generate if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\",\"    end else if (CPA_SPLIT) begin : g_split\")\r\ns=s.replace(old,new)\r\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\r\nt=open('build/exp/top.sv').read()\r\nt=t.replace(\"    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = `SPL;\",\"    localparam bit       SEL_REG   = `SEL;\\n    localparam bit       CPA_SPLIT = `SPL;\\n    localparam bit       CPA_CSEL  = `CSL;\")\r\nt=t.replace(\"CSA_REG[3] + 1 + CPA_SPLIT;\",\"CSA_REG[3] + 1 + (CPA_SPLIT | CPA_CSEL) + SEL_REG;\")\r\nt=t.replace(\".CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT))\",\".CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .SEL_REG(SEL_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT), .CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL))\")\r\nopen('build/exp/top.sv','w').write(t)\r\nr=open('build/exp/run.sh').read()\r\nr=r.replace(\"s/\\\\`SPL/1'b$S/\\\"\",\"s/\\\\`SPL/1'b$S/; s/\\\\`SEL/1'b${SEL:-0}/; s/\\\\`CSL/1'b${CSL:-0}/\\\"\")\r\nopen('build/exp/run.sh','w').write(r)\r\nEOF\r\ngrep -n \"^sed\" build/exp/run.sh; grep -n \"LAT_M  \\|SEL_REG\\|CSEL\" build/exp/top.sv | head\r\nfor cfg in \"1 1111 0 1\" \"0 1111 0 1\" \"1 0101 0 1\"; do set -- $cfg; sed \"s/\\`PRE/1'b1/; s/\\`ENC/1'b0/; s/\\`CSA/4'b$2/; s/\\`SPL/1'b$3/; s/\\`SEL/1'b$1/; s/\\`CSL/1'b$4/\" build/exp/top.sv > build/exp/ft/top.sv; iverilog -g2012 -s mkMultBuff_tb -P mkMultBuff_tb.CLK_HALF_NS=0.625 -o build/exp/ft/a.vvp submission/testbench/rtl_checker.sv starter/rtl/memory_wrapper_2port.sv starter/rtl/registerArray.sv build/exp/ft/top.sv build/exp/mult_pipe.sv 2>&1 | grep -v -i warn | head -3; echo \"cfg $cfg: $(vvp -n build/exp/ft/a.vvp | grep -E '^(ALL PASS|FAIL)|latency=')\"; done\r\n7:sed \"s/\\`PRE/1'b${PRE:-1}/; s/\\`ENC/1'b$E/; s/\\`CSA/4'b$C/; s/\\`SPL/1'b$S/; s/\\`SEL/1'b${SEL:-0}/; s/\\`CSL/1'b${CSL:-0}/\" build/exp/top.sv > $D_DIR/rtl/mkMultBuff.sv\r\n24:    localparam bit       SEL_REG   = `SEL;\r\n26:    localparam bit       CPA_CSEL  = `CSL;\r\n27:    localparam int       LAT_M     = 1 + (PRE_ENC ? 0 : ENC_REG) + CSA_REG[0] + CSA_REG[1] + CSA_REG[2] + CSA_REG[3] + 1 + (CPA_SPLIT | CPA_CSEL) + SEL_REG;\r\n58:    mult_pipe #(.PRE_ENC(PRE_ENC), .ENC_REG(ENC_REG), .CSA_REG(CSA_REG), .SEL_REG(SEL_REG), .CPA_SPLIT(CPA_SPLIT), .CPA_CSEL(CPA_CSEL))\r\ncfg 1 1111 0 1: ==== mkMultBuff_tb summary (seed=402, period=1.250 ns, latency=8, cycles=5862) ====\r\nALL PASS\r\ncfg 0 1111 0 1: ==== mkMultBuff_tb summary (seed=402, period=1.250 ns, latency=7, cycles=5897) ====\r\nALL PASS\r\ncfg 1 0101 0 1: ==== mkMultBuff_tb summary (seed=402, period=1.250 ns, latency=6, cycles=5894) ====\r\nALL PASS\r\n"]
[2043.453, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m (SEL=1 CSL=1 PRE=1 build/exp/run.sh i800a 1.25 0 1111 0 1000 0 kogge-stone & SEL=0 CSL=1 PRE=1 build/exp/run.sh i800b 1.25 0 1111 0 1000 0 kogge-stone & wait) 2>&1 | grep -v Warning; SEL=1 CSL=1 PRE=1 build/exp/run.sh i800c 1.25 0 0101 0 1000 0 kogge-stone 2>&1 | grep -v Warning; for d in i800a i800b i800c; do echo \"== $d\"; build/exp/path.sh build/exp/$d/sta.rpt | sed -n '3,30p' | head -14; done\r\ni800a P=1.25 enc=0 csa=1111 spl=0 abcD=1000 | yosys_area=5094.698000 rsz_area=5413 wns=-0.610 whs=0.028 pwr_est=2.9950e-03\r\ni800b P=1.25 enc=0 csa=1111 spl=0 abcD=1000 | yosys_area=4254.138000 rsz_area=5072 wns=-0.779 whs=0.028 pwr_est=2.5716e-03\r\ni800c P=1.25 enc=0 csa=0101 spl=0 abcD=1000 | yosys_area=4343.514000 rsz_area=4848 wns=-1.468 whs=0.028 pwr_est=2.5540e-03\r\n== i800a\r\n_4513_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=6 d=0.477 t=0.477\r\n_2860_/ZN (OAI221_X2) fo=1 d=0.109 t=0.587\r\n_2861_/ZN (OAI33_X1) fo=3 d=0.517 t=1.104\r\n_4203_/ZN (NOR4_X1) fo=1 d=0.107 t=1.211\r\n_4207_/ZN (NOR3_X4) fo=1 d=0.196 t=1.407\r\n_4208_/ZN (XNOR2_X2) fo=4 d=0.159 t=1.566\r\n_4215_/ZN (AND3_X2) fo=1 d=0.170 t=1.736\r\n_4216_/ZN (NOR3_X4) fo=1 d=0.030 t=1.766\r\n                                     1.766   data arrival time\r\n                           -0.094    1.156   library setup time\r\n                                    -1.766   data arrival time\r\nslack (VIOLATED) fo=-0.610 d= t=\r\n== i800b\r\n_3986_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=4 d=0.491 t=0.491\r\n_2389_/ZN (AOI22_X4) fo=3 d=0.105 t=0.597\r\n_2392_/ZN (NOR3_X2) fo=4 d=0.256 t=0.853\r\n_2393_/ZN (NOR3_X1) fo=3 d=0.087 t=0.940\r\n_2394_/ZN (NOR3_X1) fo=2 d=0.304 t=1.243\r\n_2407_/ZN (AOI22_X1) fo=3 d=0.133 t=1.377\r\n_3575_/ZN (OAI221_X2) fo=1 d=0.206 t=1.583\r\n_3576_/ZN (OAI21_X1) fo=1 d=0.083 t=1.666\r\n_3577_/Z (MUX2_X1) fo=1 d=0.193 t=1.859\r\n_3578_/Z (BUF_X4) fo=1 d=0.082 t=1.941\r\n                                     1.941   data arrival time\r\n                           -0.087    1.163   library setup time\r\n                                    -1.941   data arrival time\r\nslack (VIOLATED) fo=-0.779 d= t=\r\n== i800c\r\n_4153_/Q (DFF_X1) fo=5 d=0.500 t=0.500\r\n_2343_/ZN (XNOR2_X2) fo=2 d=0.175 t=0.675\r\n_2344_/ZN (XNOR2_X2) fo=5 d=0.198 t=0.873\r\n_2363_/ZN (NOR2_X2) fo=6 d=0.083 t=0.956\r\n_2427_/ZN (OAI33_X1) fo=2 d=0.432 t=1.387\r\n_2428_/ZN (AOI21_X2) fo=5 d=0.127 t=1.514\r\n_2440_/ZN (AOI211_X4) fo=2 d=0.377 t=1.892\r\n_2446_/ZN (OR4_X2) fo=3 d=0.088 t=1.980\r\n_3555_/Z (MUX2_X1) fo=1 d=0.245 t=2.224\r\n_3564_/ZN (NAND4_X4) fo=2 d=0.090 t=2.315\r\n_3565_/Z (MUX2_X1) fo=1 d=0.234 t=2.549\r\n_3566_/Z (BUF_X4) fo=1 d=0.082 t=2.631\r\n                                     2.631   data arrival time\r\n                           -0.087    1.163   library setup time\r\n"]
